<title>USA: Drier into weekend for flood-hit Europe -WSC.</title>
<headline>Drier into weekend for flood-hit Europe -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central and northeastern Europe should have drier weather into the weekend giving more favourable conditions for the flood clean-up along the Oder River, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Central and eastern Europe would have scattered showers. These would diminish in Germany on Sunday, WSC said.</p>
